// SAM System Commands

// Help and Information
+ (help|what can you do|commands|show commands|assist me|what commands|available commands)
- Here are the commands I can help you with! I can manage files, control services, run system commands, and much more. ::::: help :::::

+ (status|how are things|system status|check status|system check|how is everything)
- Let me check the system status for you. ::::: status :::::

+ (services|what services|running services|list services|show services|service list)
- I'll show you all available services. ::::: services :::::

+ (version|what version|sam version|show version|check version|current version)
- Let me show you the current SAM version. ::::: version :::::

+ (errors|show errors|error log|check errors|any errors|system errors)
- I'll display the error output for you. ::::: errors :::::

+ (clear|clear screen|cls|clear my screen|clear the screen|clean screen|empty screen|refresh screen)
- Clearing the screen for you. ::::: clear :::::

+ (exit|quit|bye|goodbye|terminate|stop|close|shutdown|end)
- Goodbye! Exiting the command prompt. ::::: exit :::::

// File Operations
+ (ls|list files|show files|what files|files|list directory|directory contents|show directory|what is here|what files are here|dir|directory listing)
- I'll list the files in the current directory. ::::: ls :::::

+ (ls la|list all files|show all files|detailed files|detailed listing|list all|show all|hidden files|all files|detailed view)
- Showing detailed file listing with hidden files. ::::: ls -la :::::

+ (ls l|detailed list|long listing|detailed format|file details|show details)
- Showing detailed file listing. ::::: ls -l :::::

+ (ls a|show hidden|hidden files|list hidden|include hidden|all including hidden)
- Showing all files including hidden ones. ::::: ls -a :::::

+ (pwd|where am i|current directory|working directory|current location|my location|where am i now|current path|show path)
- Let me show you the current directory. ::::: pwd :::::

+ cd *
- Changing to directory <star>. ::::: cd <star> :::::

