// Error handling and help
+ i need help with *
- I'd be happy to help you with <star>. Can you be more specific about what you need?

+ how do i *
- To <star>, I can help guide you. What specifically would you like to do?

+ (how to *|help with *|assist with *|guide for *)
- I can help you with <star>. What would you like to know specifically?

+ * not working
- It sounds like <star> isn't working properly. Let me help you troubleshoot this. You might want to check the status first.

+ * error
- I see you're having an error with <star>. Can you tell me more about what's happening?

+ (something is wrong|having problems|need troubleshooting|system issues)
- I'm here to help! Can you describe what problem you're experiencing?

+ (cant *|cannot *|unable to *|wont *)
- I understand you're having trouble with <star>. Let me help you figure this out.

// Common variations and shortcuts
+ (l|list|dir)
- Listing current directory contents. ::::: ls :::::

+ (la|ll|detailed)
- Showing detailed directory listing. ::::: ls -la :::::

+ (h|home)
- Going to home directory. ::::: cd ~ :::::

+ (b|back|up)
- Going up one directory level. ::::: cd .. :::::

+ (q|quit|exit)
- Goodbye! ::::: exit :::::

+ (c|cls|clean)
- Clearing the screen. ::::: clear :::::

// Friendly conversational patterns
+ (thanks|thank you|great|awesome|perfect)
- You're welcome! Is there anything else I can help you with?

+ (hi|hello|hey|greetings)
- Hello! I'm here to help you with system commands. What would you like to do?

+ (good morning|good afternoon|good evening)
- Good day! How can I assist you with your system today?

+ (what can you do|your capabilities|what are you|who are you)
- I'm SAM, your system assistant! I can help you with file operations, system monitoring, service management, and much more. Just ask me naturally, like "show me files" or "start the web server".

+ (nice|cool|impressive|good job)
- Thank you! I'm always here to help make your system tasks easier.
